// Dwelling conditions (L. 821-2, L. 822-3/R. 822-1, R. 821-2, R. 822-23/25,
// R. 842-14, R. 844-4/5, L. 823-3): main-residence recognition, the 10 %
// owner-share defeater, the required floor area with its foyer/chambre
// tracks, the family-care compatibility marker, and the six L. 823-3 sums
// deemed rent (the assimilated sum feeds loyer_principal for the calculation).
//
// EFFECT ON THE RIGHT: the surface and owner-share defeaters below target
// 03's droit_ouvert (already defeasible); they fire only on their own new
// facts, so all pre-existing scenarios are unaffected. residence_principale_
// reconnue is ADVISORY (03 keeps reading occupation_residence_principale);
// wiring it as a gate is an owner follow-up.
// R. 822-24 (decency criteria in decree 2002-120) has no rule here: its
// criteria live in an unpinned decree and the mechanism stays the 03
// judgment channel (declared despite in source-manifest.json).
//
// FRAGMENTS (predicted): base + all 7 _ED per cited article (all stable
// since 2019-09-01). L. 822-3 reuses its EXISTING fragments.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.apl version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:apl";

use self::{
    CCH_L821_2,
    CCH_L821_2_ED2019_12,
    CCH_L821_2_ED2020_01,
    CCH_L821_2_ED2021_01,
    CCH_L821_2_ED2023_04,
